.Dd November 13, 2026
.Dt NETD 8
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm netd
.Nd RavenBSD net: socket server over loopback and virtio-net
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm /sbin/netd
.Op nic
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
runs the native socket core with IPv4 loopback configured
.Pq Li 127.0.0.1/8 ,
registers the
.Dq net:
scheme and serves one file per socket plus the
.Pa net:
control file.
.Pp
When the persistent
.Dq nic:
frame service is available,
.Nm
maps its B39 shared ring and adds a second core for the virtio-net interface
.Dq eth0
.Pq Li 10.0.2.15/24 , gateway 10.0.2.2 .
The optional
.Ar nic
argument makes the NIC mandatory: the server exits if the service cannot be
attached.  Without it the server retries once a second while running so a
driver that starts later is still picked up.  IPv6 is not configured.
.Pp
Scheme paths are:
.Bl -tag -width "net:tcp/<ipv4>:<port>" -compact
.It Pa net:
interface control channel
.It Pa net:tcp/ Ns Ar ipv4 : Ns Ar port
TCP socket; the path endpoint is the listener endpoint for
.Dv LISTEN
and the remote endpoint for
.Dv CONNECT
.It Pa net:udp/ Ns Ar ipv4 : Ns Ar port
UDP socket
.El
.Pp
After
.Dv OPEN ,
the client uses the S11
.Dv CALL
operation with a
.Xr raven-proto-net 3
.Dv SocketRequest
message.  The supported calls are
.Dv BIND ,
.Dv LISTEN ,
.Dv ACCEPT ,
.Dv CONNECT ,
.Dv SHUTDOWN ,
.Dv GETSOCKNAME ,
.Dv GETPEERNAME ,
.Dv SETSOCKOPT ,
.Dv GETSOCKOPT
and
.Dv EVENT .
A successful
.Dv ACCEPT
returns a numeric socket id; the client opens
.Pa net:accept/<id>
to materialise the SchemeFile handle for that connection.  This is the
ABI-v1 substitute for an S25 attachment: there is no server-side file-create
primitive, so the accepted descriptor is opened explicitly.  B12b may replace
it with the standard attachment path when the protocol grows one.
.Pp
.Dv READ
and
.Dv WRITE
move stream bytes for TCP.  A typed
.Dv SocketRequest::Read
returns a
.Dv Response::Read
header followed by the datagram payload and the source endpoint for UDP;
.Dv SocketRequest::Write
carries an optional destination endpoint.  A raw UDP write is accepted only
after
.Dv CONNECT
sets a peer.
.Pp
.Dv EVENT
returns an S25
.Dv UserEvent
attachment in the
.Dv CALL
reply.  The client registers that handle in an S26 event queue and waits for
readable, writable, accepted or closed transitions rather than retrying with
sleeps.  The server itself blocks in
.Dv EVQ_WAIT
on the scheme-server handle and uses the stack's next-timer delay as the
timeout, so stack timers still run without a heartbeat thread.  When
.Dq eth0
is attached the loop also drains the NIC rings at least every 10 ms; both
cores are driven by the same loop and there is no per-device thread.
.Pp
.Dv TCP_NODELAY
is applied to the native TCP socket.
.Dv SO_REUSEADDR ,
.Dv SO_RCVBUF
and
.Dv SO_SNDBUF
are retained per socket and reported back by
.Dv GETSOCKOPT ;
the native stack in this revision has no per-socket bind or buffer knob, so
those values do not alter stack behaviour yet.
.Pp
The control file accepts
.Dv IfaceRequest
messages.
.Dv LIST
returns
.Dq lo
and, when attached,
.Dq eth0 ;
.Dv ARP_LIST
returns an empty table;
.Dv SET_ADDRESS
and
.Dv SET_STATE
update the selected interface, while route operations return
.Er EOPNOTSUPP .
Socket paths under
.Li 127.0.0.0/8
use the loopback core; every other path uses the NIC core when it is attached.
.Pp
The server polls the native stacks after each request and after each event
wakeup; clients sleep only when they do not ask for a readiness event.
The loopback qtest uses a client/server pair inside one probe process, waits on
the
.Dv EVENT
doorbells, checks TCP and UDP bytes, the accept path, local/peer endpoints,
socket options and orderly close, lists
.Dq lo ,
restarts
.Nm
once through
.Xr svcctl 1 ,
and runs the same probe again to show that the socket table was released.
.Pp
The
.Dq netd-virtio
qtest boots
.Xr virtio-net 8
and
.Nm ,
then sends TCP and UDP payloads through the QEMU user-mode gateway; the TCP
side uses a QEMU
.Dv guestfwd
.Dq /bin/cat
echo and the UDP side uses a one-shot host echo bound to the gateway alias.
It restarts
.Nm
between the two probe runs and checks that the ring is remapped and both
payloads still echo.  There is no host bridge or external network.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/services.d/netd.toml -compact
.It Pa /etc/services.d/netd.toml
service manifest
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr svcctl 1 ,
.Xr init 8 ,
.Xr vfsd 8 ,
.Xr virtio-net 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
server first appeared in RavenBSD 0.1.
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD ABI v1; `raven-proto-net` protocol version 1.
